{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPEVeiMnNv1f3317e7Ak","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I graded F8 as **partly**, matched to planted problem **P3** (due dates promised without a capacity check), and saved `grade.json`.\n\n- **Right effect:** the finding picks out the two late-delivery spikes the key plants. In the warehouse, order jobs with a weld operation shipped on time 0.8016 of the time in 2016 and 0.851 in 2021, against 0.9846–0.9978 in every other year. Jobs without weld fell to 0.9154 in 2016 and 0.7898 in 2021 (t442). Its conclusion that 2016 was a delay inside the plant, not a material problem, is consistent with this.\n- **Cause missing:** it never reaches the planted cause. Due dates come from a standard lead time, and lines go late when the bottleneck work centre is loaded. The finding says it could not tell which work centre held jobs, and it attributes about 0.39 of the 2021 excess to longer vendor lead times instead.\n- **Limit of the check:** the truth tables have no capacity or lateness table. The true hours by work centre are dated by operation completion and don't settle the bottleneck question on their own. Weld ran 50,379 h in 2016 and 47,166 h in 2021, against 42,488–49,672 h in other years (t443).\n\nThe finding's material-timing and slack figures do not match any other planted problem, so they don't change the grade."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":661,"cache_read_input_tokens":30687,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":661},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55c1cda4-a913-4835-9016-68daad33d25f","uuid":"73a92bfc-1b07-4769-a808-384307ef06e0","timestamp":"2026-10-